==German==
===Etymology===
Late Latin ''[[anatomia]]'' [[dissection]], from Greek ''[[άνατέμνειν]]'' to [[dissect]], from ''[[άνα-]]'' + ''[[τέμνειν]]'' to [[cut]]

===Noun===
'''Anatomie''' {{f}}
# {{biology|lang=de}} [[anatomy]], [[study]] of the [[structure]] of [[living]] [[being]]s
# {{biology|lang=de}} [[dissection]]
# {{biology|lang=de}} [[structural]] [[makeup]] of an [[organism]] or parts thereof
# [[anatomy department]], [[anatomical institute]]
# [[treatise]] on the [[science]] of [[anatomy]]

